Drop the diagnostic-suppressing pragmas that R CMD check notes

R CMD check reports every file containing `#pragma GCC|clang diagnostic
ignored` ("Files which contain pragma(s) suppressing diagnostics"), and a
CRAN reviewer may ask for them to go. Two upstream files carry them:

  lib/constant_time_impl.h  push/ignore/pop of -Wredundant-decls around the
                            whole header, whose static inline functions are
                            deliberately declared in constant_time_internal.h
                            and defined here.
  lib/platform_util.c       push/ignore/pop of -Wvla around the compiler
                            barrier after mbedtls_platform_zeroize(), whose
                            asm operand casts to a variable-length array type.

Neither warning is in -Wall, -Wextra or -pedantic under C99 or later, which
is what CRAN compiles with, so neither fires without the pragmas. Measured
before this patch was written: all 18 vendored sources compile with 0
warnings under -std=gnu99, gnu17 and gnu23 (gnu2x for GCC) with
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic, on Apple clang 17 and GCC 14; and
tools:::.check_pragmas() finds 2 files before the patch and 0 after.

Only the preprocessor blocks that exist to hold the pragmas are removed. The
zeroisation barrier and every constant-time function are unchanged, and the
MSVC `#pragma warning` lines in constant_time_impl.h stay: they are not
compiled by any R toolchain and R CMD check does not match them.

Local, not upstream: upstream builds with -Wredundant-decls and -Wvla on and
needs these. Re-check this patch applies on every release bump; it is two
deletion-only hunks plus a comment each.

--- a/lib/constant_time_impl.h
+++ b/lib/constant_time_impl.h
@@ -27,10 +27,10 @@
  * Disable -Wredundant-decls so that gcc does not warn about this. This is re-enabled
  * at the bottom of this file.
  */
-#if defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC) && (__GNUC__ > 4)
-    #pragma GCC diagnostic push
-    #pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wredundant-decls"
-#endif
+/* zucrypt: the push/ignore of -Wredundant-decls that stood here, and the
+ * pop at the bottom, are removed by tools/patches/tf-psa-crypto/0002
+ * (R CMD check notes any diagnostic pragma). -Wredundant-decls is in
+ * neither -Wall, -Wextra nor -pedantic, so nothing warns without them. */
 
 /* armcc5 --gnu defines __GNUC__ but doesn't support GNU's extended asm */
 #if defined(MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM) && defined(__GNUC__) && (!defined(__ARMCC_VERSION) || \
@@ -505,10 +505,5 @@
 {
     return (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) (~x);
 }
-
-#if defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC) && (__GNUC__ > 4)
-/* Restore warnings for -Wredundant-decls on gcc */
-    #pragma GCC diagnostic pop
-#endif
 
 #endif /* TF_PSA_CRYPTO_CONSTANT_TIME_IMPL_H */
--- a/lib/platform_util.c
+++ b/lib/platform_util.c
@@ -101,21 +101,13 @@
         /* For clang and recent gcc, pretend that we have some assembly that reads the
          * zero'd memory as an additional protection against being optimised away. */
 #if defined(__clang__) || (__GNUC__ >= 10)
-#if defined(__clang__)
-#pragma clang diagnostic push
-#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wvla"
-#elif defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC)
-#pragma GCC diagnostic push
-#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wvla"
-#endif
+        /* zucrypt: upstream wraps this line in pragmas silencing -Wvla,
+         * removed by tools/patches/tf-psa-crypto/0002 (R CMD check notes any
+         * diagnostic pragma). -Wvla is in neither -Wall, -Wextra nor
+         * -pedantic under C99 and later, so nothing warns without them. */
         asm volatile ("" : : "m" (*(char (*)[len]) buf) :);
-#if defined(__clang__)
-#pragma clang diagnostic pop
-#elif defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC)
-#pragma GCC diagnostic pop
 #endif
 #endif
-#endif
     }
 }
 #endif /* MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_ZEROIZE_ALT */
